<aside class="sync-panel" aria-labelledby="sync-heading">
 <div class="sync-heading"><div><p>Always yours to curate</p><h3 id="sync-heading">Fresh code. A considered collection.</h3></div><span id="portfolio-sync-state">Loading sync status…</span></div>
 <p>New public GitHub repositories arrive as private drafts. Your project edits, publication choices and deleted entries are preserved. Review each draft, complete its story, then publish when ready.</p>
 <p class="sync-meta" id="portfolio-sync-schedule">Weekly discovery · Public repositories only · No automatic publishing</p>
 <div class="sync-actions"><button id="portfolio-sync-run" type="button" disabled>Sync this week</button><button id="portfolio-sync-toggle" type="button" disabled>Pause sync</button><a href="https://github.com/ghwmelite-dotcom?tab=repositories" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View GitHub repositories <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
 <p id="portfolio-sync-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
 <div id="portfolio-sync-history"></div>
 <p class="sync-note">Forks, archived, disabled and empty repositories are excluded. Up to 20 new drafts per run; any remaining projects wait for the next weekly run. Draft descriptions come from GitHub metadata and need your review.</p>
</aside>
